  "version": 1,
  "title": "Dimension and identifiability of three-sunlet models",
  "abstract": "Normalized Latin systems of every order m at least five have three-sunlet image dimension 5m-4 in every characteristic, including the original finite abelian-group coordinates. Two transitive derangement families give the stated dimension 3m+2c-2. Complex generic fibers have unique unordered toric decomposition, normalized degree twice the square of the loop abelianization order, and the character-wreath Galois group. The model is rational over Q. Prime nonassociative loops give precisely two normalized general preimages; cyclic models of every order at least six admit rational reconstruction from the literal 8m-12 retained coordinates. Orbit and inverse-stable partition identifications have the complete dimension classification, which yields the full binary level-one network formula including triangles and two leaves.",
